"""Derive SkyyZones/build_skyyzones_0.3.2.py from SkyyZones/build_skyyzones_0.3.1.py (the tools/deploy_set.py SET pin, generated by
tools/zones_0_3_1_patch.py - never re-run that one for this). Edit THIS patch, never the generated script. Every anchor is asserted; at the
end every change is undone on a copy and compared with 0.3.1 (tools/soundpass_gen.Patch). Line endings kept.
Run:  python tools/zones_0_3_2_patch.py   then   python SkyyZones/build_skyyzones_0.3.2.py   (never --deploy)
Harness: python SkyyZones/test_skyyzones_0.3.2.py [--keep]

0.3.2 = Skyy's first whole-island gathering test (skywynn_zones2, 2026-10-25) + four scope adds from the main session the same day.
Skyy's words (docs/answered/world.md, 2026-10-25): "i cant gather dirt, stones, rubble, plants," + "or this tree" (a giant autumn tree near
Drifting Plains; "A red message") -> popup "Dirt + grass (regrow), Stone + rubble (regrow), Plants + flowers (regrow)"; "also cant mine the
crystals" (red / orange crystal clusters in a cave there); "can you make the zone wand visualize the box?"; "i don't need to set mining
zones, and foraging zones, because everywhere is a gating and combat zone. so i need save zones where monsters dont spawn. and the town
zones where you cant gather, and no monsters spawn."
 1. THE BIG TREE (root cause, reproduced on the real vanilla prefabs - tools/dev/scratch/zones032/sim/treesim.py replays ZFell.search on
    all 1138 Server/Prefabs/Trees prefabs): every autumn tree (Trees/Autumn/Stage_1-3, orange Plant_Leaves_Autumn) is OAK wood, and about
    40 % of its trunk - most of the thick lower trunk - is Wood_Oak_Trunk_Full (Autumn_Stage3_004: 140 Trunk_Full + 201 other wood pieces).
    The 'logs' type listed Wood_*_Trunk / _Branch_* / _Roots but NOT Wood_*_Trunk_Full (0.3.0 fixer 2 thought _Full pieces were built,
    but they are in the engine's own TreeWood.json list and in every big vanilla tree), so a hit on a Trunk_Full block was "not a resource
    block" -> the red "You can only gather the marked resource blocks here." It was NOT the skill gate (no gate on logs), NOT the size
    (an autumn tree is ~1,100 blocks, 4,700 search reads) and NOT a region. Fix: 'logs' = Wood_*_Trunk,Wood_*_Trunk_Full,Wood_*_Branch_*,
    Wood_*_Roots; the build now FAILS if any id of TreeWood.json is not matched by the logs line. Also from the replay: the biggest vanilla
    tree (Oak Stage 8, 8,466 blocks) was over tree.maxBlocks 6000 -> "This tree is too big to regrow": default 9000 (all 1138 prefabs fit;
    the biggest search reads 20,552 cells, far under the 60,000 cap).
 2. NEW GATHER TYPES (vanilla ids from Assets.zip, every pattern checked against the vanilla item list at build): dirt (dirt / grass / mud /
    leaf litter soils, never _Half / _Stairs / Tilled), clay (raw coloured clay, never bricks / smooth / cobble), sand (sand + gravel),
    ice (snow block, ice, permafrost), rock (the natural rocks the 0.2.0 stone line missed: red / white sandstone, aqua, salt, dawnstone,
    cooled magma, cracked volcanic), rubble (Rubble_* + pebbles), crystals (Rock_Crystal_* - every colour, clusters + blocks: Skyy's cave),
    cave (stalactites / icicles, moss, cave roots), plants (grass tufts, ferns, flowers, bushes, vines, reeds, seaweed, cactus, petals,
    brambles, barnacles, coral), mushrooms (small mushrooms - caps, common, flatcaps, glowing, shelves; NOT the giant mushroom block
    parts and not boomshrooms). Left out on purpose: tree fruit (hangs on trees - a later orchard round), lavender / sunflower (farm crops
    with stages), hay (built), every _Half / _Stairs / brick / smooth / cobble / decorative variant (built by players or prefabs). 'stone'
    joins gather.types too (Skyy: "everywhere is a gathering ... zone"; the 0.3.0 Q8 "stone only in mine regions" is replaced).
    Regrow (Server Setup -> Zones -> Regrowing blocks table, seconds): stone 3 (as before), rock 3, dirt 8, clay 8, sand 8, ice 8,
    rubble 10, cave 20, plants 20, crystals 30 (like gems), mushrooms 30. Placeholder: full blocks (dirt, clay, sand, ice, rock, stone)
    Rock_Bedrock like the ores; small / see-through things (rubble, crystals, cave, plants, mushrooms) 'Empty' = the spot stays open
    (a cube of bedrock where a flower was would look wrong). Drops: vanilla. A regrow never overwrites anything: it is written only while
    the spot still holds its placeholder (Empty = air), and never into a player (0.2.0 rule). Gates: none on the new types.
    F-PICK (new): flowers / plants / mushrooms are picked with F in vanilla (Gathering Harvest = an F 'harvest' our guard counts as a break):
    a pick of a listed non-crop block now records its regrow like a break (state 3: the pass looks once after 1 s - still there = the pick
    failed, entry dropped), so a picked flower grows back too (before: it was gone for good in a gathering area).
    MULTI-BLOCK parts (filler != 0): refused "Break it at its base." (before: broken like vanilla with NO regrow = a hole for good).
    PLAYER-PLACED BLOCKS (unchanged rule, read in 0.3.0 / 0.3.1): nobody places blocks in a gathering area (only Scaffolding, which vanishes);
    builder mode / zones.opBypass admins can. SkyyZones never tracks who placed a block (SkyySkills' PlacedStore is only its XP list), so a
    builder-placed dirt / stone / flower outside a town breaks and regrows like a natural one - put builds inside a town region.
 3. ONE-TIME UPDATE Mig032 (PROJECT-RULES 4; the reviewed Mig030 pattern: History copies first, one Changes line per key with Undo, marker
    migrate-0.3.2.done, the file's bytes + line endings kept, a java.util.Properties check that nothing else differs): types.properties -
    type.logs rewritten ONLY while it holds the 0.3.1 default, the 10 new types appended when absent; regen.properties - their regrow rows
    appended when absent; config.properties - gather.types rewritten ONLY while it holds the 0.3.1 default (Skyy's file has NO gather.types
    line - the kit appended only zones.gatherWorlds - so the new built-in default applies there with no file change); trees.properties -
    tree.maxBlocks 6000 -> 9000 only while 6000. Hand-edited lines are kept and logged.
 4. ZONE KINDS (Skyy: safe zones + towns): three region kinds - TOWN (= the old FULL; 'full' still works and is what the file keeps, so a
    0.3.1 rollback reads towns unchanged), SAFE (new, file word 'safe': gathering as if no region were there - the world's rules apply -
    and NO monster spawns), SKYBLOCK (kept for old mine regions). /zones region create <name> town|safe|skyblock. NO SPAWNS in towns + safe
    zones (Server Setup -> Zones -> Protection 'No monster spawns in towns + safe zones', default ON): a RefSystem on NPCEntity removes, the
    moment it is added, a NATURAL world spawn (AddReason.SPAWN + NPCEntity.getEnvironment() set - only WorldSpawnJobSystems.preAddToWorld
    sets it; quest / merchant / pet / shard NPCs spawned by code and prefab spawn markers never have it) whose WorldSupport attitude is
    HOSTILE and whose role is not a harmless vanilla animal (birds, fish, critters, livestock, Kweebecs, temple NPCs: the role folders of
    Server/NPC/Roles, list built at build time). Mobs that WALK IN stay (only spawning is blocked - recommended, no mob is ever deleted in
    front of a player); chunk loads (AddReason.LOAD) are never touched. SkyyMobs has no spawns of its own (it levels vanilla spawns) - so
    nothing to change there now; for later rounds the bridge question zones:fn:noSpawn {world, x, y, z} -> Boolean is published (Mobs /
    WorldGen follow-up: ask it before a custom spawn).
 5. WAND OUTLINE (Skyy: "make the zone wand visualize the box"): while an admin HOLDS the Zone Wand, every 1 s (to that player only): the
    selected box (corner A alone = that block; A + B = the box) as particle lines on all 12 edges, plus up to 4 region boxes within 48
    blocks, each kind in its own colour (town red, safe green, skyblock cyan, mine = a skyblock region with stone / ore / crystal types
    white). Cost: at most 80 points for the selection + 40 per region box (<= 240 particles a second per wand holder, admins only); stops
    the moment the wand leaves the hand. Server Setup -> Zones -> Titles + tools: 'Zone Wand outline' on/off + the five particle ids.
 UNVERIFIED (needs the game): the colours of the five vanilla particle systems; a NATURAL spawn removed in onEntityAdded leaves no trace
 (the spawner just tries again later); breaking sand / gravel next to more sand (falling blocks fall before the placeholder is written?);
 a plant / sand standing on a dug-out dirt block pops off by engine physics (no event) and does not come back (only the dirt does).
 ROLLBACK to 0.3.1: (1) delete every SAFE region first (/zones region delete <name>) - 0.3.1 reads 'safe' as a bad line and then locks the
 whole world FULL; (2) /zones restore all, wait for "0 waiting" (0.3.1 has no regrow row for the new types: their waiting blocks would use
 regen.defaultSec + bedrock); the new type / regrow lines and migrate-0.3.2.done may stay (0.3.1 then lets those types break in SKYBLOCK
 regions that list them, nothing else).
"""
